$A + B = (-D - 28T) + (D - 28T) = -56T$.

$$2800 = \frac{1}{4T^2} [(-2D)(-56T)]$$
$$2800 = \frac{112DT}{4T^2} = \frac{28D}{T}$$

Solving for $T$:
